% Pressure Reducing Support Surfaces: the three LCDs L33830 (Group 1),
% L33642 (Group 2) and L33692 (Group 3) and their Policy Articles A52489,
% A52490 and A52468 (DME MACs), one program. A policy program of the DMEPOS
% model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category, prior
% authorization, continued need, refills) and states when a claim for a
% Group 1 mattress overlay or mattress (E0181, E0182, E0184, E0185, E0186,
% E0187, E0188, E0189, E0196, E0197, E0198, E0199, A4640), a Group 2 surface
% (E0193, E0277, E0371, E0372, E0373) or a Group 3 air-fluidized bed (E0194)
% is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the three Group 1 criteria (complete
% immobility; limited mobility with one of the conditions A-D; a pressure
% ulcer on the trunk or pelvis with one of the conditions A-D), the three
% Group 2 criteria (multiple stage 2 ulcers on the trunk or pelvis that
% failed to improve over a month of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program
% on a Group 1 surface; large or multiple stage 3 or 4 ulcers on the trunk
% or pelvis; a myocutaneous flap or skin graft within 60 days after a Group
% 2 or 3 surface in the hospital or nursing facility), the continued use of
% a Group 2 surface or a Group 3 bed until the ulcer is healed, and the
% Group 3 criteria (a stage 3 or 4 ulcer; bedridden or chair bound; would
% otherwise be institutionalized; a month of conservative treatment on a
% Group 2 surface without progression, evaluated within a month before the
% bed; a trained caregiver; the treating practitioner directing the regimen
% and recertifying monthly; every alternative ruled out; no
% contraindication). The payment condition it adds (Policy Article A52468):
% the treating practitioner's monthly statement for an air-fluidized bed,
% kept on file by the supplier.
%
% How the criteria are read. Ulcers are what the record states, as numbers:
% "Ann has 2 pressure ulcers of stage 3 on pelvis" (the count, the stage of
% the LCDs' appendix as a number, the site: trunk, pelvis, or another site
% such as heel), so that "multiple" (at least 2, summed over the record's
% lines), "stage 3 or 4" and "on the trunk or pelvis" are in the rules. The
% mobility criteria are the record's statements in the LCDs' own words
% ("cannot make changes in body position without assistance"; "cannot
% independently make changes in body position significant enough to
% alleviate pressure"; "bedridden or chair bound as a result of severely
% limited mobility"): complete immobility and limited mobility are graded
% descriptions of one state, not two judgments, and as two findings one
% would always leave a judgment open beside the other's answer. The
% conditions A-D of Group 1 and the contraindications of Group 3 are
% documented conditions (the shared template "the medical record of B
% documents C") from the lists below; the treatment programs are dated
% events with their required elements, like the standard written order of
% dmepos.le. The findings this policy reads (the judged template of
% dmepos.le, "the finding F about B is established" or unsupported, with who
% found it and why), and the criterion each stands for:
%   large ulcer (Group 2 criterion 2: "large or multiple" — consulted only
%   when the record does not show multiple ulcers); surface necessary for
%   wound management (Group 2 and 3 continued use, alternative 2 — consulted
%   only when the record shows neither healing nor a modified care plan);
%   institutionalization otherwise required (Group 3: "In the absence of an
%   air-fluidized bed, the beneficiary would require institutionalization");
%   alternative equipment ruled out (Group 3: "All other alternative
%   equipment has been considered and ruled out").
% Therapy with an air-fluidized bed is taken to start on the day the bed is
% delivered. One month is read as 30 days, and the monthly recertification
% window as 31 days (a calendar month between two dates of service), LE
% having day arithmetic only.
%
% Not modelled: that the record documents the severity of a condition A-D
% "sufficiently to demonstrate the medical necessity" (the documented
% condition is read as documented at that severity); that the beneficiary
% does not "bottom out" on the surface and the coding characteristics of
% the Policy Articles (coding, carried by the HCPCS code); the care plan
% "there should be" for a Group 2 surface; the occlusive barrier "required,
% when necessary" and the wet-to-dry dressing rules of Group 3; the "other
% known contraindications" and the caregiver "unwilling or unable" (the
% record's statement that a trained caregiver is available stands for the
% contrary); the KX, GA and GZ modifiers.
%
% ICD-10 tables. The Policy Articles A52490 and A52468 list covered
% diagnoses (sources/icd10/A52490_icd10_covered.csv,
% A52468_icd10_covered.csv, one group each: Group 1 of A52490 serves E0193,
% E0277, E0371, E0372, E0373; Group 1 of A52468 serves E0194). They are not
% loaded: they add nothing to the LCDs' text — A52490's codes are the
% pressure ulcers of the back, hip, buttock, sacral region and contiguous
% sites (the trunk or pelvis) of stages 2, 3, 4 and unstageable, which the
% LCD states as the ulcer's stage and site; A52468's are the stage 3 and 4
% pressure ulcers of every site (elbow, back, hip, buttock, ankle, heel,
% head, other), confirming that Group 3 restricts the stage and not the
% site. Unstageable ulcers (an obscured stage 3 or 4 in the LCDs' appendix)
% are stated with the stage they are revealed to be. Article A52489 (Group
% 1) has no table.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record: mobility and the ulcers
    *a beneficiary* cannot make changes in body position without assistance; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* cannot independently make changes in body position significant enough to alleviate pressure; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* is bedridden or chair bound as a result of severely limited mobility; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has *a number* pressure ulcers of stage *a second number* on *a site*; undefined.
    the pressure ulcers of *a beneficiary* failed to improve over the past month; undefined.
    the pressure ulcers of *a beneficiary* have healed; undefined.
    the pressure ulcers of *a beneficiary* are progressing toward healing; undefined.
    the care plan of *a beneficiary* is being modified to promote healing; undefined.
    % the record: the treatment programs, the surgery, the bed
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of *a beneficiary* began on *a date*; undefined.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of *a beneficiary* includes *an element*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* had a myocutaneous flap or skin graft for a pressure ulcer on *a site* on *a date*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* was on a group *a number* support surface immediately prior to discharge from *a facility* on *a date*; undefined.
    the course of conservative treatment of *a beneficiary* began on *a date*; undefined.
    the course of conservative treatment of *a beneficiary* included *an element*; undefined.
    the pressure ulcers of *a beneficiary* showed no progression toward healing during the course of conservative treatment; undefined.
    the treating practitioner evaluated *a beneficiary* for *an item* on *a date*; undefined.
    a trained adult caregiver is available to assist *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    the treating practitioner directs the home treatment regimen of *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    the treating practitioner recertified the need for *an item* in a monthly statement dated *a date*; undefined.
    the supplier holds the monthly treating practitioner statements for *an item*; undefined.
    % derived
    *an item* is a group 1 support surface.
    *an item* is a group 2 support surface.
    *an item* is an air fluidized bed.
    *a beneficiary* meets the group 1 coverage criteria.
    *a condition* is a group 1 qualifying condition.
    *a beneficiary* has a pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis.
    *a beneficiary* meets the group 2 coverage criteria for *a claim*.
    *a beneficiary* has multiple stage 2 pressure ulcers on the trunk or pelvis.
    *a beneficiary* has large or multiple stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcers on the trunk or pelvis.
    *a beneficiary* has a stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis.
    *a beneficiary* has a stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer.
    *a beneficiary* has been on a comprehensive ulcer treatment program for a month before *a claim*.
    *an element* is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program.
    the continued use criteria are met for *a claim*.
    continued use of a support surface is justified for *a beneficiary*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the air fluidized bed coverage criteria for *an item*.
    *a beneficiary* completed a course of conservative treatment before the evaluation for *an item*.
    the evaluation of *a beneficiary* for *an item* is timely.
    *an element* is a required element of conservative treatment.
    *a beneficiary* has a contraindication to an air fluidized bed.
    *a condition* is a contraindication to an air fluidized bed.
    the monthly recertification is documented for *a claim*.

the knowledge base support surfaces includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base support surfaces includes:

LCD L33830 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33830".
the text of LCD L33830 is at "sources/lcd/L33830.txt".
LCD L33642 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33642".
the text of LCD L33642 is at "sources/lcd/L33642.txt".
LCD L33692 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33692".
the text of LCD L33692 is at "sources/lcd/L33692.txt".
Policy Article A52489 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52489".
the text of Policy Article A52489 is at "sources/article/A52489.txt".
Policy Article A52490 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52490".
the text of Policy Article A52490 is at "sources/article/A52490.txt".
Policy Article A52468 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52468".
the text of Policy Article A52468 is at "sources/article/A52468.txt".

% What the surfaces are, by code: the Group 1 overlays and mattresses (the
% LCD), the Group 2 surfaces and the air-fluidized bed (the Policy Articles'
% coding guidelines).
rule ss_group_1_codes with provenance LCD L33830,
        confer "A Group 1 mattress overlay or mattress ( E0181, E0182, E0184, E0185, E0186, E0187, E0188, E0189, E0196, E0197, E0198, E0199 and A4640) is covered if one of the following three criteria are met":
an item is a group 1 support surface
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0181", "E0182", "E0184", "E0185", "E0186", "E0187", "E0188", "E0189", "E0196", "E0197", "E0198", "E0199", "A4640"].

rule ss_group_2_codes with provenance Policy Article A52490,
        confer "Heavy duty and bariatric devices are included in the codes for pressure reducing support surfaces: E0193, E0277, E0371, E0372 and E0373":
an item is a group 2 support surface
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0193", "E0277", "E0371", "E0372", "E0373"].

rule ss_group_3_codes with provenance Policy Article A52468,
        confer "An air-fluidized bed (E0194) is a device employing the circulation of filtered air through silicone coated ceramic beads creating the characteristics of fluid":
an item is an air fluidized bed
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0194".

% The ulcers of the record: any ulcer on the trunk or pelvis (Group 1
% criterion 3), a stage 3 or 4 ulcer on the trunk or pelvis (Group 2
% criterion 2, "large"), a stage 3 or 4 ulcer anywhere (Group 3).
rule ss_ulcer_trunk_pelvis with provenance LCD L33830,
        confer "The beneficiary has any stage pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis":
a beneficiary has a pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis
    if the beneficiary has a number pressure ulcers of stage a second number on a site
    and the number >= 1
    and the site is in [trunk, pelvis].

rule ss_ulcer_stage_3_4_trunk_pelvis with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "large or multiple stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer(s) on the trunk or pelvis":
a beneficiary has a stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis
    if the beneficiary has a number pressure ulcers of stage a second number on a site
    and the number >= 1
    and the second number is in [3, 4]
    and the site is in [trunk, pelvis].

rule ss_ulcer_stage_3_4 with provenance LCD L33692,
        confer "The beneficiary has a stage 3 (full thickness tissue loss) or stage 4 (deep tissue destruction) pressure ulcer":
a beneficiary has a stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer
    if the beneficiary has a number pressure ulcers of stage a second number on a site
    and the number >= 1
    and the second number is in [3, 4].

% The conditions A-D of Group 1 (criteria 2 and 3).
impaired nutritional status is a group 1 qualifying condition,
    as stated in LCD L33830, confer "Impaired nutritional status".
fecal incontinence is a group 1 qualifying condition,
    as stated in LCD L33830, confer "Fecal or urinary incontinence".
urinary incontinence is a group 1 qualifying condition,
    as stated in LCD L33830, confer "Fecal or urinary incontinence".
altered sensory perception is a group 1 qualifying condition,
    as stated in LCD L33830, confer "Altered sensory perception".
compromised circulatory status is a group 1 qualifying condition,
    as stated in LCD L33830, confer "Compromised circulatory status".

% The elements of the comprehensive ulcer treatment program (Group 2
% criterion 1), each of them required.
use of an appropriate group 1 support surface is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program,
    as stated in LCD L33642, confer "Use of an appropriate group 1 support surface".
regular assessment by a licensed healthcare practitioner is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program,
    as stated in LCD L33642, confer "Regular assessment by a nurse, practitioner, or other licensed healthcare practitioner".
appropriate turning and positioning is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program,
    as stated in LCD L33642, confer "Appropriate turning and positioning".
appropriate wound care is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program,
    as stated in LCD L33642, confer "Appropriate wound care".
appropriate management of moisture and incontinence is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program,
    as stated in LCD L33642, confer "Appropriate management of moisture/incontinence".
nutritional assessment and intervention is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program,
    as stated in LCD L33642, confer "Nutritional assessment and intervention consistent with the overall plan of care".

% The elements conservative treatment "must include" (Group 3). The three it
% "should generally include" (education of the beneficiary and caregiver,
% assessment at least weekly, management of moisture/incontinence) are not
% required.
frequent repositioning is a required element of conservative treatment,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Frequent repositioning of the beneficiary with particular attention to relief of pressure over bony prominences (usually every 2 hours)".
use of a group 2 support surface is a required element of conservative treatment,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Use of a Group 2 support surface to reduce pressure and shear forces on healing ulcers and to prevent new ulcer formation".
treatment of wound infection is a required element of conservative treatment,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Necessary treatment to resolve any wound infection".
optimization of nutrition status is a required element of conservative treatment,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Optimization of nutrition status to promote wound healing".
debridement is a required element of conservative treatment,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Debridement by any means, including wet-to-dry gauze dressings, to remove devitalized tissue from the wound bed".
maintenance of a moist wound bed is a required element of conservative treatment,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Maintenance of a clean, moist bed of granulation tissue with appropriate moist dressings protected by an occlusive covering, while the wound heals".

% The circumstances that deny an air-fluidized bed, as documented conditions.
coexisting pulmonary disease is a contraindication to an air fluidized bed,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "The beneficiary has coexisting pulmonary disease".
unprotected moist wound dressings is a contraindication to an air fluidized bed,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "The beneficiary requires treatment with wet soaks or moist wound dressings that are not protected with an impervious covering such as plastic wrap or other occlusive material".
inadequate structural support for the bed is a contraindication to an air fluidized bed,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Structural support is inadequate to support the weight of the air-fluidized bed system".
insufficient electrical system is a contraindication to an air fluidized bed,
    as stated in LCD L33692, confer "Electrical system is insufficient for the anticipated increase in energy consumption".

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: durable medical
% equipment (each Policy Article).
rule ss_codes with provenance Policy Article A52489,
        confer "Pressure-reducing support surfaces are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is support_surfaces
    if the code is in ["E0181", "E0182", "E0184", "E0185", "E0186", "E0187", "E0188", "E0189", "E0196", "E0197", "E0198", "E0199", "A4640", "E0193", "E0277", "E0371", "E0372", "E0373", "E0194"].

section applicability is:

rule ss_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52489,
        confer "Pressure-reducing support surfaces are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is support_surfaces.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Group 1: an overlay or mattress, one of three criteria.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ss_group_1 with provenance LCD L33830,
        confer "A Group 1 mattress overlay or mattress ( E0181, E0182, E0184, E0185, E0186, E0187, E0188, E0189, E0196, E0197, E0198, E0199 and A4640) is covered if one of the following three criteria are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a group 1 support surface
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the group 1 coverage criteria.

% Criterion 1.
rule ss_group_1_immobile with provenance LCD L33830,
        confer "The beneficiary is completely immobile - i.e., beneficiary cannot make changes in body position without assistance":
a beneficiary meets the group 1 coverage criteria
    if the beneficiary cannot make changes in body position without assistance.

% Criterion 2.
rule ss_group_1_limited_mobility with provenance LCD L33830,
        confer "The beneficiary has limited mobility - i.e., beneficiary cannot independently make changes in body position significant enough to alleviate pressure and at least one of conditions A-D below":
a beneficiary meets the group 1 coverage criteria
    if the beneficiary cannot independently make changes in body position significant enough to alleviate pressure
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a group 1 qualifying condition.

% Criterion 3.
rule ss_group_1_ulcer with provenance LCD L33830,
        confer "The beneficiary has any stage pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis and at least one of conditions A-D below":
a beneficiary meets the group 1 coverage criteria
    if the beneficiary has a pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a group 1 qualifying condition.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Group 2: a powered or advanced surface, one of three criteria, and the
% continued use rule after the first month.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ss_group_2 with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "A group 2 support surface is covered if the beneficiary meets at least one of the following three Criteria (1, 2 or 3)":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a group 2 support surface
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the group 2 coverage criteria for the claim
    and the continued use criteria are met for the claim.

% Criterion 1: multiple stage 2 ulcers, a month of the program, no improvement.
rule ss_group_2_criterion_1 with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "The beneficiary has multiple stage 2 pressure ulcers located on the trunk or pelvis":
a beneficiary meets the group 2 coverage criteria for a claim
    if the beneficiary has multiple stage 2 pressure ulcers on the trunk or pelvis
    and the pressure ulcers of the beneficiary failed to improve over the past month
    and the beneficiary has been on a comprehensive ulcer treatment program for a month before the claim.

% "multiple": at least two, over the record's lines
rule ss_multiple_stage_2 with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "multiple stage 2 pressure ulcers located on the trunk or pelvis":
a beneficiary has multiple stage 2 pressure ulcers on the trunk or pelvis
    if a total is the sum of each N such that
        the beneficiary has a number N pressure ulcers of stage 2 on a site
        and the site is in [trunk, pelvis]
    and the total >= 2.

% the month of the program before the date of service, with each element
rule ss_treatment_program with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "which have failed to improve over the past month, during which time the beneficiary has been on a comprehensive ulcer treatment program including each of the following":
a beneficiary has been on a comprehensive ulcer treatment program for a month before a claim
    if the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of the beneficiary began on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 30
    and for all cases in which
            an element is a required element of a comprehensive ulcer treatment program
        it is the case that
            the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of the beneficiary includes the element.

% Criterion 2: large or multiple stage 3 or 4 ulcers.
rule ss_group_2_criterion_2 with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "The beneficiary has large or multiple stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer(s) on the trunk or pelvis":
a beneficiary meets the group 2 coverage criteria for a claim
    if the beneficiary has large or multiple stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcers on the trunk or pelvis.

% "multiple" is a count of the record; "large" a judgment, consulted only
% when the record does not show multiple ulcers (the "otherwise" is this
% model's device, so that a count the record establishes does not leave a
% judgment open beside it).
rule ss_large_or_multiple with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "large or multiple stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer(s) on the trunk or pelvis":
a beneficiary has large or multiple stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcers on the trunk or pelvis
    if a total is the sum of each N such that
        the beneficiary has a number N pressure ulcers of stage a second number S on a site
        and S is in [3, 4]
        and the site is in [trunk, pelvis]
    and the total >= 2
    otherwise the beneficiary has a stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis
    and the finding large ulcer about the beneficiary is established.

% Criterion 3: a flap or graft within 60 days, after a Group 2 or 3 surface
% in the hospital or nursing facility left within 30 days.
rule ss_group_2_criterion_3 with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "The beneficiary had a myocutaneous flap or skin graft for a pressure ulcer on the trunk or pelvis within the past 60 days":
a beneficiary meets the group 2 coverage criteria for a claim
    if the beneficiary had a myocutaneous flap or skin graft for a pressure ulcer on a site on a date
    and the site is in [trunk, pelvis]
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 60
    and the beneficiary was on a group a second number support surface immediately prior to discharge from a facility on a third date
    and the second number is in [2, 3]
    and the facility is in [hospital, nursing facility]
    and the other date is a third number days after the third date
    and the third number >= 0
    and the third number <= 30.

% Continued use (Group 2 and Group 3 alike; LCD L33692: "Continued use of an
% air fluidized bed is covered until the ulcer is healed or, if healing does
% not continue, there is documentation to show that"): the first claim needs
% nothing beyond the coverage criteria; a later rental month needs the ulcer
% not healed, and healing continuing or the documentation of (1) or (2).
% the first claim is not an ongoing claim: a device of this model
rule ss_first_claim:
the continued use criteria are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is an ongoing claim.

rule ss_continued_use with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "Continued use of a group 2 support surface is covered until the ulcer is healed, or if healing does not continue, there is documentation in the medical record to show that":
the continued use criteria are met for a claim
    if the claim is an ongoing claim
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the pressure ulcers of the beneficiary have healed
    and continued use of a support surface is justified for the beneficiary.

% healing continues; otherwise (1) "other aspects of the care plan are being
% modified to promote healing"; otherwise (2) "the use of the group 2 support
% surface is reasonable and necessary for wound management" — a judgment,
% consulted only when the record shows neither (the "otherwise" is this
% model's device).
rule ss_continued_use_justified with provenance LCD L33642,
        confer "other aspects of the care plan are being modified to promote healing":
continued use of a support surface is justified for a beneficiary
    if the pressure ulcers of the beneficiary are progressing toward healing
    otherwise the care plan of the beneficiary is being modified to promote healing
    otherwise the finding surface necessary for wound management about the beneficiary is established.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Group 3: an air-fluidized bed, all criteria, the monthly recertification,
% the continued use rule.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ss_group_3 with provenance LCD L33692,
        confer "An air-fluidized bed is covered only if all of the following criteria are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an air fluidized bed
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the air fluidized bed coverage criteria for the item
    and the monthly recertification is documented for the claim
    and the continued use criteria are met for the claim.

% The criteria: the ulcer ("The beneficiary has a stage 3 (full thickness
% tissue loss) or stage 4 (deep tissue destruction) pressure ulcer"), the
% mobility, the institutionalization, the conservative treatment and the
% evaluation, the caregiver, the practitioner directing the regimen, the
% alternatives, no contraindication.
rule ss_air_fluidized_criteria with provenance LCD L33692,
        confer "The beneficiary is bedridden or chair bound as a result of severely limited mobility":
a beneficiary meets the air fluidized bed coverage criteria for an item
    if the beneficiary has a stage 3 or 4 pressure ulcer
    and the beneficiary is bedridden or chair bound as a result of severely limited mobility
    and the finding institutionalization otherwise required about the beneficiary is established
    and the beneficiary completed a course of conservative treatment before the evaluation for the item
    and the evaluation of the beneficiary for the item is timely
    and a trained adult caregiver is available to assist the beneficiary
    and the treating practitioner directs the home treatment regimen of the beneficiary
    and the finding alternative equipment ruled out about the beneficiary is established
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary has a contraindication to an air fluidized bed.

% The course of conservative treatment: at least a month before the
% evaluation, each required element, no progression toward healing.
rule ss_conservative_treatment with provenance LCD L33692,
        confer "The course of conservative treatment must have been at least one month in duration without progression toward wound healing":
a beneficiary completed a course of conservative treatment before the evaluation for an item
    if the course of conservative treatment of the beneficiary began on a date
    and the treating practitioner evaluated the beneficiary for the item on an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 30
    and the pressure ulcers of the beneficiary showed no progression toward healing during the course of conservative treatment
    and for all cases in which
            an element is a required element of conservative treatment
        it is the case that
            the course of conservative treatment of the beneficiary included the element.

% The evaluation within a month before the bed is delivered (therapy starts
% with the delivery).
rule ss_evaluation_timely with provenance LCD L33692,
        confer "The evaluation generally must be performed within one month prior to initiation of therapy with the air-fluidized bed":
the evaluation of a beneficiary for an item is timely
    if the treating practitioner evaluated the beneficiary for the item on a date
    and the item was delivered on an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 30.

rule ss_contraindication with provenance LCD L33692,
        confer "An air-fluidized bed will be denied as not reasonable and necessary under any of the following circumstances":
a beneficiary has a contraindication to an air fluidized bed
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a contraindication to an air fluidized bed.

% The monthly recertification: a statement of the treating practitioner
% within the month before each rental month after the first; the first month
% has the order and the evaluation.
rule ss_monthly_recertification with provenance LCD L33692,
        confer "A treating practitioner directs the home treatment regimen, and reevaluates and recertifies the need for the air-fluidized bed on a monthly basis":
the monthly recertification is documented for a claim
    if the claim is an ongoing claim
    and the claim is for an item
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the treating practitioner recertified the need for the item in a monthly statement dated an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 31.

% the first month is certified by the order and the evaluation: a device of
% this model
rule ss_first_month_certified:
the monthly recertification is documented for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is an ongoing claim.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own condition of payment: for an air-fluidized bed, the
% treating practitioner's monthly statement on file with the supplier.
% Groups 1 and 2 add nothing to the general requirements (their Policy
% Articles state no policy specific requirement): a device of this model.
rule ss_documentation_groups_1_2:
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is support_surfaces
    and the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the item is an air fluidized bed.

rule ss_documentation_air_fluidized with provenance Policy Article A52468,
        confer "This monthly treating practitioner statement must be kept on file by the supplier and be available for inspection upon request":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is support_surfaces
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is an air fluidized bed
    and the supplier holds the monthly treating practitioner statements for the item.
